# National Girlfriend Day Website Rules

## Project Overview

Build a premium-quality, mobile-first GitHub Pages website for my long-distance girlfriend.

This should NOT feel like a generic website.

It should feel like opening a beautifully designed iPhone app or interactive digital scrapbook.

The overall experience should be emotional, polished, elegant, and memorable.

The target audience is ONE person.

Everything should prioritize beauty over showing off technical complexity.

---

# Tech Stack

Use:

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

No frameworks unless absolutely necessary.

Optimize for GitHub Pages.

Everything should be static.

No backend.

No database.

No external dependencies that could easily break.

---

# Mobile First

This website is designed primarily for iPhone Safari.

Desktop should still work, but mobile is the priority.

Every screen should fit naturally on an iPhone.

Avoid desktop interactions like hover effects.

Use touch-friendly buttons.

Support swipe gestures.

Animations should be smooth at 60fps.

---

# Overall Theme

The visual style should resemble:

- Apple-quality UI
- Premium iOS app
- Midnight sky
- Deep navy gradients
- Soft stars
- Paper scrapbook
- Warm handwritten notes

Think:

Opening someone's private journal at midnight.

NOT:

A Valentine's Day template.

Avoid cheesy designs.

Avoid bright reds.

Avoid excessive hearts.

Use hearts sparingly.

---

# User Flow

The experience should be:

Envelope

↓

Welcome Page

↓

Disclaimers

↓

Interactive Scrapbook

↓

Gift Box

↓

Gift Reveal

↓

Final Goodbye

There should never be a confusing navigation menu.

The experience should naturally flow from beginning to end.

---

# Envelope

The website opens with a beautiful envelope.

Text:

To:
May

Happy (Almost) National Girlfriend Day!

From:
Ben

The envelope should have a satisfying opening animation.

Only after opening should the rest of the experience begin.

---

# Welcome Page

Include:

Hi May ❤️

Happy (Almost) National Girlfriend Day!

I know we haven't known each other forever, but I wanted to make something that we could look back on later.

This isn't every memory we've had together—just some of my favorites.

A button:

Start Reading →

---

# Disclaimers

Show two tasteful cards.

Card 1

Everything on this website uses Ben Standard Time (PST).

Sorry Japan ❤️

Card 2

These definitely aren't all of our memories.

These are simply some of my favorite moments that I wanted to remember forever.

---

# Scrapbook

The scrapbook is the main feature.

Each page should feel handcrafted.

Include:

- paper texture
- tape
- photo
- handwritten title
- handwritten date
- small decorations
- page number

Photos should automatically crop into attractive squares.

Support horizontal swiping between pages.

Every scrapbook page should fill the screen.

Keep text readable.

Never overcrowd the page.

---

# Memories

Create pages using the supplied data.

Stories should remain short.

Maximum:

2–3 sentences.

The handwritten date belongs near the bottom.

---

# Gift Box

The gift box should feel like opening a real present.

Use two password screens.

Lock One

Question:

What is my phone password?

Answer:

nby8ryu3

Lock Two

Question:

What is my middle name?

Answer:

michael

Do NOT expose answers in page source unless unavoidable.

Once unlocked:

Beautiful opening animation.

Confetti.

Gift coupon.

---

# Coupon

Display a premium coupon.

Title:

One Free Meal ❤️

Value:

Up to ¥5000

Redeem Instructions:

Text Ben:

not icecream

Include a Copy Code button.

---

# Final Screen

Fade into a starry night.

Slow typewriter animation.

Display:

See you again soon.

Love,

Ben

No buttons.

No restart.

Let the moment breathe.

---

# Animations

Prioritize quality.

Use:

- spring animations
- page fades
- subtle scaling
- paper movement
- realistic easing

Avoid flashy animations.

No spinning objects.

No excessive bouncing.

---

# Performance

Images should lazy-load.

Compress assets.

Maintain smooth scrolling.

Everything should feel fast on an iPhone.

---

# Accessibility

Large tap targets.

Readable fonts.

Good contrast.

Responsive layouts.

---

# Code Quality

Organize code cleanly.

Separate HTML, CSS, and JS.

Comment major sections.

Make it easy to add or edit scrapbook pages later.

---

# Design Philosophy

Every design decision should answer:

"Would this make May smile?"

If yes, keep it.

If not, simplify it.

Quality is more important than quantity.
